Model Checkpoint for MCTS Interpretation
This repository provides a pre-trained Chemprop v1 model checkpoint for Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS)–based molecular interpretation. The checkpoint file (.pt or .ckpt) contains the complete model architecture and learned parameters, enabling direct application without retraining.

Usage
To employ the checkpoint in MCTS interpretation, load the model via the MPNN.load_from_file() API and integrate it as the scoring function within the MCTS workflow. The model predicts property scores for candidate substructures, guiding the tree search toward chemically meaningful rationales.
Compatibility Requirements

Version: The checkpoint must be generated by Chemprop v1.
Task type: Ensure alignment between the checkpoint's training objective (classification or regression) and the interpretation target.
Input format: The model accepts single-molecule SMILES strings; additional atom/bond features are not supported in the current MCTS implementation.
Citation
If you use this checkpoint in your research, please cite the appropriate Chemprop version and the original MCTS methodology
